      "text": "Since \\[\\sqrt[3]{x} + \\sqrt[3]{20 - x} = 2,\\]square both sides to obtain\n\\[x + 2\\sqrt[3]{20x - x^2} + 20 - x = 4 + 8\\sqrt[3]{20x - x^2}.\\](Canceling like terms and rearranging yields)\n\\[20 - 2x = 8\\sqrt[3]{20x - x^2},\\quad \\text{i.e.}\\quad 10 - x = 4\\sqrt[3]{20x - x^2}.\\]\nNow, cubes both sides to obtain\n\\[1000 - 10x + x^3 = 64(20x - x^2).\\](Rearrange to get a cubic equation, and let \\\\(y = x^3.\\) Then, this simplifies to \\\\(y^3 - 67y - 200 = 0.\\) The quadratic factorization of the latter gives us \\\\((y - 10)(y^2 + 10y + 20) = 0;\\) by the factor theorem, \\\\(y = 10\\\\) is the only real root.\n\nNow substituting back, we obtain \\\\(x = 10 - 2 = 8.\\\\) Thus, the smaller value is \\\\(\\boxed{18}.\\)",
